**(a) Ask for a budget.** Ask in plain text, then end the turn. Offer these four options with these exact labels, and name the current budget when the file records one. With no models file, name the budget whose effort matches the defaults in step 5.

=== entry 6b1ae68d1673
kind: translation
rules: setup-pstack, model-role
intent: A budget sets each entry's effort to its level, or the highest that model offers below it; drops slug parsing, the `auto` alias, and the Grok/Claude slug examples. Keep "keep the user's changed roles on a re-run" and "mark a role needing a choice".
--- upstream
**(b) Apply it.** Build the working table from the skill defaults, and on a re-run keep any role you changed by family, list, or alias (`inherit-parent`, `auto`). `unlimited`, `large`, `medium`, and `small` set the effort token of every real slug, panel entries included, to `max`, `xhigh`, `high`, or `medium`. The effort token is the last token, or the one before a trailing `fast`, on the ladder `max` > `xhigh` > `high` > `medium` > `low`. If the result is not a detected slug, use the same family's detected slug with the highest effort at or below the target, else mark the role as needing a choice. `inherit-parent` and `auto` do not change. So `unlimited` turns `claude-opus-5-5-xhigh` into `claude-opus-5-5-max`. Grok slugs top out at `xhigh`, so under `unlimited` the fallback puts Grok at `xhigh` and keeps `grok-4.7-xhigh-fast` as it is. `large` keeps both defaults. `small` turns them into `claude-opus-5-5-medium` and `grok-4.7-medium-fast`.
--- patched
**(b) Apply it.** Build the working table from the defaults, and on a re-run keep any role you changed by model, list, or alias (`inherit-parent`). `unlimited`, `large`, `medium`, and `small` set the effort of every real entry, panel entries included, to `max`, `xhigh`, `high`, or `medium`, on the ladder `max` > `xhigh` > `high` > `medium` > `low`. Ignore effort options off that ladder. If the model doesn't offer that effort, use the highest effort it offers below it, else mark the role as needing a choice. `inherit-parent` does not change. So under `unlimited`, a model whose efforts stop at `xhigh` runs at `xhigh`.

=== entry a5142a367fd3
kind: translation
rules: ask, setup-pstack, model-role, cursor-only
intent: Confirms roles in plain text with `inherit-parent` as the only alias; drops `auto` and Cursor's Auto. Keep the panel-list, cross-judge (one judge, other-family values in list order, inherit-parent never judges), and swarm notes.
--- upstream
**(c) Show the roles and confirm.** Show every role with its model, marking any real slug not in the detected set as needing a choice. Also list each line step 2 dropped. Ask whether to accept as-is or change specific roles, offering the detected models plus `inherit-parent` and `auto` (both mean: this role runs on the parent chat model, which is how Auto users stay on Auto) as the options. Prefer AskQuestion over free text. For panel roles (arena runners, architect runners, interrogate reviewers) the value is a list, and one subagent runs per entry, alias entries included, so the list length sets the count. `arena cross-judge pool` is also a list, but Arena runs one judge. It tries only values from a family other than the parent's, in list order, so order it by preference. An `inherit-parent` or `auto` value never judges. `swarm workers` is the default model for every worker unless a race or comparison assigns another model per arm.
--- patched
**(c) Show the roles and confirm.** Show every role with its entries, marking any real entry not in the detected set as needing a choice. Also list each line step 2 dropped. Ask whether to accept as-is or change specific roles, offering the detected models plus `inherit-parent` (this role runs on the parent chat model) as the options. Ask in plain text, then end the turn. For panel roles (arena runners, architect runners, interrogate reviewers) the value is a list, and one subagent runs per entry, alias entries included, so the list length sets the count. `arena cross-judge pool` is also a list, but Arena runs one judge. It tries only values from a family other than the parent's, in list order, so order it by preference. An `inherit-parent` value never judges. `swarm workers` is the default model for every worker unless a race or comparison assigns another model per arm.

